            "review_title": "Review at Social Local - Beer N' Bite",
            "review_text": "Anthony\n2 contributions\n0\nDirectly insulted and humiliated by the wait staff\nMay 2022 • Friends\nMe and my friends were having drinks there on a Monday night. We didn’t have any problems with the food or the drink or the night in general but when it came time to pay the bills, a staff member brought them over, each bill for each member of the group. One of the females in our group noticed the word “mập” written at the top of her bill. She’s a white woman but speaks and reads Vietnamese quite well. For those of you who don’t know, it means “fat”. She questioned the waiter as to why he wrote that. He said “it means the person who’s bill it belongs to”. She again asked him what it said and he continued to refuse to say the word, only till she said she knew what it meant, he then admitted it said fat and that he wrote it. \nI’ve travelled around the world, to different continents and many countries and never seen anything so inconsiderate and feral in my life, from someone in the service industry.\nFor full transparency of this situation, we were initially offered a 70k discount from our bill ($3 US) as an apology, till we phoned the manager of the restaurant (not on site) to explain what happened, who then offered a full refund of our bill ($25 US). \n\nIf you want to go to a bar and be body shamed, humiliated and directly insulted by the wait staff, definitely go have a drink here. Enjoy the experience of being served by Vietnamese staff who are happy to pass judgement on their customers and refer to us by whatever insulting label they see fit to use, and who think that white people are stupid enough not to understand a language other than their own.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 25, 2022",
            "rating": 5.0,
